---
/** The Discord bot: how to add it, what each command does, what an
 * answer shows, and what it does not do. The bot is its own repository;
 * this page is the front door. */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const APP_ID = "1549899039384797244";
/** Discord's own install link for the app: it reads the installation
 * contexts set on the app, so one link offers both a server and an
 * account install. */
const install = `https://discord.com/oauth2/authorize?client_id=${APP_ID}`;
const commands: [string, string][] = [
  ["/card name", "A card, with its default printing's art. Start typing and pick from the suggestions; pressing enter on free text takes the best match."],
  ["/id C000230", "A card by its codex id, or one physical printing by its printing id (/id P000937): that printing's own art, set, product, finish, artist and flavour text."],
  ["/random", "A random card. The embed says which printing it is showing."],
  ["/search query", "The first five matches for a query in the search syntax, each with its art, the total, and a button to all results on this site."],
  ["/syntax", "The search syntax on one screen, shown to you alone."],
  ["/history name", "Every face the card has had, oldest first, each change against the one before: mana, stats, thresholds, rules text before and after, and any earlier names."],
  ["/set name", "A set by name or code: release date, how many cards and printings, some of its cards, and a search for all of them."],
  ["Find cards", "Right-click any message, open Apps and pick Find cards: every [[card name]] in that message, up to five, with their art. A message with no brackets is tried as one name."],
];
---
<Base title="Discord bot" canonical="/discord" description="Kairos Archive's Discord bot: card lookups, printings, histories, sets and searches in any server, with the same data and syntax as this site.">
  <h1>Discord bot</h1>
  <p>Kairos Archive's bot answers card questions inside Discord with the same data and the same search syntax as this site. Slash commands only: it never reads messages, never posts unprompted, and stores nothing.</p>

  <h2>Add it</h2>
  <p><a class="btn" href={install}>Add to Discord</a></p>
  <p>Discord asks where to add it. <strong>A server</strong> needs the Manage Server permission there and makes the commands available to everyone in it. <strong>Your account</strong> lets you use the commands in any server or direct message, whether or not that server has the bot. The bot asks for no permission beyond registering its commands.</p>

  <h2>Commands</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{commands.map(([cmd, what]) => <tr><td><code>{cmd}</code></td><td>{what}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>Flipping through printings and results</h2>
  <p>A card answer carries a menu of the card's printings when it has more than one. Pick one and the message becomes that printing: its own art, artist, flavour text, and a note when it was printed with earlier values. Search results carry <strong>Next 5</strong> and <strong>Previous</strong> buttons that turn the page in place. Anyone in the channel can use them, not only whoever asked.</p>

  <h2>What an answer shows</h2>
  <p>A card embed carries the type line as printed (<em>Minion — Ordinary Giant</em>), mana, threshold drawn with the game's element symbols, power (attack and defense when they differ), life, the sets it appears in, which printing is pictured (<em>Shown: Gothic · Booster · Standard, art by Dan Seagrave</em>), the card's ids (<code>C000927 · P002719</code>), the rules text, and buttons to the card's page here and its JSON record. A double-faced card gets a second embed for its back face. A card with recorded errata says so.</p>
  <p>A search shows up to five matches as small embeds with their art, the total above them, and how many more cards mention the words only in their rules text. The <strong>All results</strong> button opens the same query on this site.</p>

  <h2>Searching from Discord</h2>
  <p><code>/search</code> takes the full <a href="/syntax">search syntax</a>: <code>t:minion e:fire cost&lt;=2</code>, <code>a:"Drew Tucker" unique:prints</code>, <code>is:errata sort:cost</code>. <code>/syntax</code> shows the short version without leaving Discord. A query the parser cannot read comes back to you alone with the reason.</p>

  <h2>Where the answers come from</h2>
  <p>Cards come from the newest verified <a href="/docs/releases">registry release</a>, read directly from <a href="/docs/endpoints">the API</a>; searches run through the <a href="/docs/query">query API</a>. A new release reaches the bot within minutes with no update on your side. The bot is open source: <a href="https://github.com/sadkinglabs/kairos-bot">sadkinglabs/kairos-bot</a>, a Cloudflare Worker you can also run yourself.</p>

  <h2>Credit</h2>
  <p>Card names, text and images are © <a href="https://sorcerytcg.com">Erik's Curiosa</a>, shown with credit for archive, identification and site function. Identifiers, structure and the bot's code are Kairos Archive's, free for any use; see <a href="/usage">usage</a>.</p>
</Base>
